cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GPEC, please cite it as below, together with the papers behind the modules you use (listed under references and on the documentation's citations page)."
type: software
version: "2.0.0"
title: "GPEC: Generalized Perturbed Equilibrium Code"
abstract: "GPEC is an open-source Julia reimplementation of the Fortran GPEC suite (DCON, VACUUM, STRIDE, GPEC, PENTRC and SLAYER), consolidated into one code base of cooperating physics modules behind a unified, modern interface. It models the response of tokamak plasmas to small non-axisymmetric magnetic perturbations: equilibrium reconstruction from EFIT, CHEASE or IMAS inputs; ideal MHD stability by Newcomb's criterion with the free-boundary vacuum response; resistive tearing stability from the outer-region Δ′ matrix matched to inner-layer models; the perturbed equilibrium driven by coils or error fields, with resonant flux, island widths and Chirikov overlap; and neoclassical toroidal viscosity torque. Applications include error-field correction, resonant magnetic perturbation optimization, kink and tearing stability, and parameter scans and integrated modeling at scale."
